  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nAn upper level trough will begin to exit the region on Tuesday, \nkeeping the area in northwesterly flow. Showers will linger on \nTuesday into Wednesday over high terrain in southwest Idaho, with \ntemperatures near normal through Wednesday. Model uncertainty \nincreases on Thursday, with some models strengthening a low pressure \nsystem over the region and bringing a push of cool air with another \nshot of moisture on Thursday and Friday. Others bring hot and dry \nconditions thanks to a building ridge of high pressure beginning as \nearly as Wednesday. Current forecast favors the warmer and drier \ntrend. By Saturday, high confidence exists in warm and dry\nconditions either continuing or returning with the ridge more \nfirmly in place through the weekend. Therefore, above normal \ntemperatures are likely Wednesday-Saturday.",
